{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Menu|Shell|audio\\\\.bus|settings\\\\.get|settings\\\\.music|screen\\\\.canvas|lastDevice|bind\\\\(' Yars-*/vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md\"","aggregated_output":"87:- 1123 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n88:- 1184 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n259:- `game.screen.canvas`: the page's canvas (null in a headless game); o: the sizing options (the game's o)\n283:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, [... omitted end of long line]\n293:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), wit [... omitted end of long line]\n303:- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Ret [... omitted end of long line]\n320:- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n321:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. E [... omitted end of long line]\n332:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n555:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n637:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game,  [... omitted end of long line]\n1070:- `game.audio.bus(name = 'sfx')`: a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument) to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute a [... omitted end of long line]\n1155:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: ! [... omitted end of long line]\n1184:## 21d. Shell\n1186:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HT [... omitted end of long line]\n1187:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) f [... omitted end of long line]\n1188:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1189:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard [... omitted end of long line]\n1190:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1191:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1628:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1718:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
