{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/src/main.js'\ns=open(p).read().replace(\\\"[['How to Play',()=>howto()],['Developer tools'\\\", \\\"[['Join second scout',()=>join()],['How to Play',()=>howto()],['Developer tools'\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"function localLobby(){\\\", \\\"function join(){if(embedded||\"'!world||world.mode!=='\"'play'||world.players.length>=2){ui.toast('Both scouts are already in flight.');return;}if(SIM.command(world,'join')){controls.setCoop(true);ui.toast('VENN has joined the swarm.','One reserve added. Devices are assigned separately.');hud();}}\\\\nfunction localLobby(){\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode --input-type=module - <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';import vm from 'node:vm';const p='Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904';const c={};vm.createContext(c);for(const f of ['content.js','sim.js'])vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(p+'/src/'+f,'utf8'),c);fs.mkdirSync(p+'/docs/presets',{recursive:true});const w=c.RuinSim.create({sector:1});const preset=c.RuinSim.exportContent(w);preset.name='GLASS WINDOW';preset.cells=preset.cells.filter(c=>c.y<245||c.y>295);fs.writeFileSync(p+'/docs/presets/glass-window.json',JSON.stringify(preset,null,2));\nJS\ncat > Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Yars of Ruin\n\nA complete three-station arcade siege campaign inspired by Yars’ Revenge (1982). You are Rill, a winged survivor. Bite a breach through a fortress shell, steal its energy, call a rail-mounted siege cannon, and get out of its way. Venn can join the same arena locally or through AI Hub.\n\nOpen the root \"'`Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904.html` directly in a browser, or this folder’s identical `index.html`. Everything is embedded; no server, assets, network connection or installation is needed for standalone play. The game uses the actual my-3D2dge 0.89.1 handoff and its native overhead renderer, Shell, input, settings, pixel art, particles and lighting. The engine and Hub client are pinned and vendored; see [provenance](docs/provenance.md).\n\nFrom this development folder:\n\n```\nnpm run build\nnpm test\n```\n\n`npm run build` regenerates the root artifact and identical development `index.html` using only Node built-ins. It embeds the pristine released AI Hub client as the first script, and safely embeds the native engine and authored source. `npm test` runs deterministic rules, drawn-headless rendering, online authority/lifecycle mocks, HTML/interview integrity, actual file-URL Chromium/WebKit input/audio/touch tests, and the official AI Hub browser harness. Only failures and a final count are printed. Evidence is retained in `tests/artifacts/`. No package installation is required. The browser runner uses the workstation’s existing Python Playwright 1.63.0 environment and downloaded browsers.\n\nFor targeted iteration after a covered change: `npm test -- --group=sim`, `online`, `presentation`, `artifact`, `browser`, or `hub`. Hub checks bind a local server to 127.0.0.1 on an OS-selected port and shut it down afterward. The full Hub group includes two ordinary-action campaign runs with a player host and a dedicated server host under latency, jitter and loss; allow a few minutes.\n\nNormal and Assist retain the full mechanic set and keep separate solo/co-op records. The campaign has three stations requiring one, two and three hits; its last hit must intercept the airborne fortress. Victory and defeat offer replay, discovered-sector practice and credits. Practice and developer changes never update normal campaign records. After ten idle menu seconds, an isolated AI demonstration plays the actual campaign and loops; any real input returns to the title.\n\nSee [controls and play](docs/controls.md), [designer guide](docs/authoring.md), [source research](docs/research.md), [art and audio](docs/art-audio.md), and [test evidence](docs/testing.md). The root `exit-interview.json` is the machine-readable report embedded in About / Credits during the build.\nEOF\ncat > Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/docs/authoring.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Authoring another defense\n\nPause during standalone play, select Developer tools, then Shield-layout editor. The encounter continues from the same simulation in a practice category. Controller focus moves between sliders and actions: choose the cell column/row, material and plate, then Place or Remove. Pointer painting is a shortcut: left paints, right removes. Plate travel/period configure vertical movement without regenerating shield occupancy. Refuge position/width changes the protected band.\n\nPreview encounter validates the data and starts it immediately. JSON import/export provides editable text and a downloadable file without a server. Save preset and Load preset store a validated encounter on this device. Invalid imports show an explanation and retain the previous working layout. The included \"'`presets/glass-window.json` is a completed two-plate example with a central opening. Paste its contents into JSON import, import it, and preview. The simulation suite also exports, reloads and wins an edited encounter with ordinary actions.\n\nA version1 encounter has these fields:\n\n| Field | Meaning / validation |\n| --- | --- |\n| `version` | Exactly1 |\n| `name` | Nonempty display name, up to60 characters |\n| `refuge: {x,w}` | x≥70, width45–220, right edge≤610 |\n| `core: {x,y,hp}` | x630–910; y40–500; integer hp1–3 |\n| `plates[]` | 1–4 unique integer IDs; `amplitude`0–90px; `period`3–40s; finite `phase` in radians; x/y retained in data |\n| `cells[]` | Up to600 individually persistent cells, absolute base x500–930, y20–520, existing `plate` ID, `material`=`normal` or `reflective`. Duplicate positions on the same plate are rejected. |\n| `pursuers` |1–3 guided threats |\n| `swirlDelay`, `swirlPeriod` | First windup5–30s; repeat7–35s |\n| `introduction` | Optional short transmission |\n\nEach plate’s sine motion offsets its cells’ base y positions. Removing a cell sets its persistent occupancy bit; moving plates never restore it. Collision and aiming use the updated position and wrapped vertical distance. A legal shot corridor must clear the projectile’s radius, not only its center.\n\nThe live balance page exposes movement speed, bite and shot cadence, bites per charge, cannon speed/windup, pursuer speed/turn rate, Swirl speed/warning, refuge outage duration and reserve count. Inputs are clamped and applied on a fixed-step boundary; Reset to Defaults restores the selected difficulty’s baseline. Freeze/Advance one tick remains operable while paused. Encounter/phase selection, restart, seed loading, spawn threat, collision overlays, invulnerability and infinite charge are available from the same tools. Gameplay editing is unavailable in AI Hub sessions.\nEOF\nmv build-info.json Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/build-info.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/src/main.js'\ns=open(p).read().replace(\\\"[['How to Play',()=>howto()],['Developer tools'\\\", \\\"[['Join second scout',()=>join()],['How to Play',()=>howto()],['Developer tools'\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"function localLobby(){\\\", \\\"function join(){if(embedded||\"'!world||world.mode!=='\"'play'||world.players.length>=2){ui.toast('Both scouts are already in flight.');return;}if(SIM.command(world,'join')){controls.setCoop(true);ui.toast('VENN has joined the swarm.','One reserve added. Devices are assigned separately.');hud();}}\\\\nfunction localLobby(){\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode --input-type=module - <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';import vm from 'node:vm';const p='Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904';const c={};vm.createContext(c);for(const f of ['content.js','sim.js'])vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(p+'/src/'+f,'utf8'),c);fs.mkdirSync(p+'/docs/presets',{recursive:true});const w=c.RuinSim.create({sector:1});const preset=c.RuinSim.exportContent(w);preset.name='GLASS WINDOW';preset.cells=preset.cells.filter(c=>c.y<245||c.y>295);fs.writeFileSync(p+'/docs/presets/glass-window.json',JSON.stringify(preset,null,2));\nJS\ncat > Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Yars of Ruin\n\nA complete three-station arcade siege campaign inspired by Yars’ Revenge (1982). You are Rill, a winged survivor. Bite a breach through a fortress shell, steal its energy, call a rail-mounted siege cannon, and get out of its way. Venn can join the same arena locally or through AI Hub.\n\nOpen the root \"'`Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904.html` directly in a browser, or this folder’s identical `index.html`. Everything is embedded; no server, assets, network connection or installation is needed for standalone play. The game uses the actual my-3D2dge 0.89.1 handoff and its native overhead renderer, Shell, input, settings, pixel art, particles and lighting. The engine and Hub client are pinned and vendored; see [provenance](docs/provenance.md).\n\nFrom this development folder:\n\n```\nnpm run build\nnpm test\n```\n\n`npm run build` regenerates the root artifact and identical development `index.html` using only Node built-ins. It embeds the pristine released AI Hub client as the first script, and safely embeds the native engine and authored source. `npm test` runs deterministic rules, drawn-headless rendering, online authority/lifecycle mocks, HTML/interview integrity, actual file-URL Chromium/WebKit input/audio/touch tests, and the official AI Hub browser harness. Only failures and a final count are printed. Evidence is retained in `tests/artifacts/`. No package installation is required. The browser runner uses the workstation’s existing Python Playwright 1.63.0 environment and downloaded browsers.\n\nFor targeted iteration after a covered change: `npm test -- --group=sim`, `online`, `presentation`, `artifact`, `browser`, or `hub`. Hub checks bind a local server to 127.0.0.1 on an OS-selected port and shut it down afterward. The full Hub group includes two ordinary-action campaign runs with a player host and a dedicated server host under latency, jitter and loss; allow a few minutes.\n\nNormal and Assist retain the full mechanic set and keep separate solo/co-op records. The campaign has three stations requiring one, two and three hits; its last hit must intercept the airborne fortress. Victory and defeat offer replay, discovered-sector practice and credits. Practice and developer changes never update normal campaign records. After ten idle menu seconds, an isolated AI demonstration plays the actual campaign and loops; any real input returns to the title.\n\nSee [controls and play](docs/controls.md), [designer guide](docs/authoring.md), [source research](docs/research.md), [art and audio](docs/art-audio.md), and [test evidence](docs/testing.md). The root `exit-interview.json` is the machine-readable report embedded in About / Credits during the build.\nEOF\ncat > Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/docs/authoring.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Authoring another defense\n\nPause during standalone play, select Developer tools, then Shield-layout editor. The encounter continues from the same simulation in a practice category. Controller focus moves between sliders and actions: choose the cell column/row, material and plate, then Place or Remove. Pointer painting is a shortcut: left paints, right removes. Plate travel/period configure vertical movement without regenerating shield occupancy. Refuge position/width changes the protected band.\n\nPreview encounter validates the data and starts it immediately. JSON import/export provides editable text and a downloadable file without a server. Save preset and Load preset store a validated encounter on this device. Invalid imports show an explanation and retain the previous working layout. The included \"'`presets/glass-window.json` is a completed two-plate example with a central opening. Paste its contents into JSON import, import it, and preview. The simulation suite also exports, reloads and wins an edited encounter with ordinary actions.\n\nA version1 encounter has these fields:\n\n| Field | Meaning / validation |\n| --- | --- |\n| `version` | Exactly1 |\n| `name` | Nonempty display name, up to60 characters |\n| `refuge: {x,w}` | x≥70, width45–220, right edge≤610 |\n| `core: {x,y,hp}` | x630–910; y40–500; integer hp1–3 |\n| `plates[]` | 1–4 unique integer IDs; `amplitude`0–90px; `period`3–40s; finite `phase` in radians; x/y retained in data |\n| `cells[]` | Up to600 individually persistent cells, absolute base x500–930, y20–520, existing `plate` ID, `material`=`normal` or `reflective`. Duplicate positions on the same plate are rejected. |\n| `pursuers` |1–3 guided threats |\n| `swirlDelay`, `swirlPeriod` | First windup5–30s; repeat7–35s |\n| `introduction` | Optional short transmission |\n\nEach plate’s sine motion offsets its cells’ base y positions. Removing a cell sets its persistent occupancy bit; moving plates never restore it. Collision and aiming use the updated position and wrapped vertical distance. A legal shot corridor must clear the projectile’s radius, not only its center.\n\nThe live balance page exposes movement speed, bite and shot cadence, bites per charge, cannon speed/windup, pursuer speed/turn rate, Swirl speed/warning, refuge outage duration and reserve count. Inputs are clamped and applied on a fixed-step boundary; Reset to Defaults restores the selected difficulty’s baseline. Freeze/Advance one tick remains operable while paused. Encounter/phase selection, restart, seed loading, spawn threat, collision overlays, invulnerability and infinite charge are available from the same tools. Gameplay editing is unavailable in AI Hub sessions.\nEOF\nmv build-info.json Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/build-info.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '471,547p' Yars-*/src/sim.js && tail -85 Yars-*/tests/hub-browser.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '471,547p' Yars-*/src/sim.js && tail -85 Yars-*/tests/hub-browser.py\"","aggregated_output":"  }\n  function exportContent(w) {\n    const data = contentFor(w);\n    return { version: 1, name: data.name || 'CUSTOM ENCOUNTER', refuge: { x: w.refuge.x, w: w.refuge.w }, core: { x: w.core.dockX, y: w.core.dockY, hp: w.core.maxHp },\n      plates: w.plates.map(({ id, x, y, amplitude, period, phase }) => ({ id, x, y, amplitude, period, phase })),\n      cells: w.cells.map(c => ({ x: c.baseX, y: c.baseY, plate: c.plate, material: c.material })),\n      pursuers: data.pursuers || 1, swirlDelay: data.swirlDelay || 14, swirlPeriod: data.swirlPeriod || 16 };\n  }\n  function pilot(w, index = 0, options = {}) {\n    /* This controller emits the exact same ordinary actions as a player. No simulation writes. */\n    const p = w.players[index]; if (!p || !p.alive || p.departed || w.mode !== 'play') return { mx: 0, my: 0, ax: 1, ay: 0, fire: false, cannon: false };\n    const core = w.core, speed = w.tuning.scoutSpeed;\n    let tx = p.x, ty = p.y, ax = 1, ay = 0, fire = true, cannon = false;\n    const final = w.sector === 2 && core.hp === 1;\n    const cannonOwn = w.cannons.find(c => c.owner === index && !c.reflected && c.life > 0);\n    const go = (x, y) => { tx = x; ty = wrap(y); };\n    const aimAt = (x, y) => { const dx = x - p.x, ddy = dy(y, p.y), len = Math.hypot(dx, ddy) || 1; ax = dx / len; ay = ddy / len; };\n    if (cannonOwn) {\n      // A real scout must leave its locked lane. Stay well clear until the projectile is spent.\n      go(p.x > 760 ? 875 : 585, cannonOwn.y + (dy(p.y, cannonOwn.y) < -1 ? -68 : 68));\n      aimAt(core.x, core.y);\n    } else if (core.state === 'phase-break') {\n      go(570, 390); aimAt(core.dockX, core.dockY);\n    } else if (!ready(w, p)) {\n      // Start by biting a center corridor. Once the shell there is open, brush the docked heart.\n      if (core.state === 'dock') {\n        go(core.x - 9, core.y);\n        const nearCell = w.cells.filter(c => c.alive && Math.abs(dy(c.y, core.y)) < 28 && c.x > p.x - 25).sort((a, b) => a.x - b.x)[0];\n        if (nearCell && p.x < core.x - 40) { go(nearCell.x, nearCell.y); fire = false; }\n        aimAt(core.x, core.y);\n      } else { go(570, 420); aimAt(core.x, core.y); }\n    } else if (final) {\n      if (core.state === 'dock') {\n        // The final heart is immune while docked. Wait outside the committed route and preserve charge.\n        go(570, core.dockY + 95); aimAt(core.x, core.y);\n      } else if (core.state === 'windup') {\n        const futureTime = Math.max(0, core.timer) + (core.x - 30) / (w.tuning.cannonSpeed - core.vx) + w.tuning.cannonWindup;\n        const futureY = wrap(core.y + core.vy * Math.max(0, futureTime - core.timer));\n        go(570, futureY); aimAt(core.x, core.y);\n        if (Math.abs(dy(p.y, futureY)) < 4 && core.timer < .12) cannon = true;\n      } else if (core.state === 'flight') {\n        const hitTime = (core.x - 30 - core.vx * w.tuning.cannonWindup) / (w.tuning.cannonSpeed - core.vx) + w.tuning.cannonWindup;\n        const targetY = wrap(core.y + core.vy * Math.max(0, hitTime));\n        go(570, targetY); aimAt(core.x, core.y);\n        if (Math.abs(dy(p.y, targetY)) < 5 && core.x > 210) cannon = true;\n      } else { go(570, 410); aimAt(core.x, core.y); }\n    } else if (core.state === 'dock') {\n      // Carve a horizontal lane with ordinary fire. Bite nearby cells first, then fire from the right flank.\n      const travel = w.tuning.cannonWindup + (core.x - 30) / w.tuning.cannonSpeed;\n      const targetY = w.sector === 2 && core.hp === 2 ? wrap(core.dockY + Math.sin((w.sectorTime + travel) * .65) * 55) : core.y;\n      const obstruction = w.cells.filter(c => c.alive && Math.abs(dy(c.y, targetY)) < 19 && c.x < core.x - 30).sort((a, b) => a.x - b.x)[0];\n      if (obstruction) {\n        go(obstruction.x - 16, obstruction.y);\n        aimAt(obstruction.x, obstruction.y);\n        fire = true;\n      } else {\n        go(585, targetY); aimAt(core.x, core.y);\n        if (Math.abs(dy(p.y, targetY)) < 4 && Math.abs(p.vy) < 65 && core.timer > travel + .1) cannon = true;\n      }\n    } else if (core.state === 'windup' || core.state === 'flight') {\n      const time = w.tuning.cannonWindup + Math.max(0, (core.x - 30 - core.vx * w.tuning.cannonWindup) / (w.tuning.cannonSpeed - core.vx));\n      const targetY = wrap(core.y + core.vy * Math.max(0, time - (core.state === 'windup' ? core.timer : 0)));\n      go(570, targetY); aimAt(core.x, core.y);\n      const clear = !w.cells.some(c => c.alive && c.x < core.x && Math.abs(dy(c.y, targetY)) < 18);\n      if (clear && Math.abs(dy(p.y, targetY)) < 4 && core.state === 'flight' && core.x > 210) cannon = true;\n    } else { go(570, 410); aimAt(core.x, core.y); }\n    // Physical danger avoidance: dodge pursuit and the transformed heart, never merely stand in fire.\n    const danger = w.hazards.filter(h => h.life > 0 && !isStatic(w, p)).map(h => ({ h, d: dist(p, h) })).sort((a, b) => a.d - b.d)[0];\n    if (danger && danger.d < 90 && !cannon) {\n      const awayY = dy(p.y, danger.h.y), awayX = p.x - danger.h.x;\n      if (Math.abs(awayY) > 8) ty = wrap(p.y + Math.sign(awayY) * 100);\n      else ty = wrap(p.y + (danger.h.vy >= 0 ? -110 : 110));\n      if (Math.abs(awayX) > 15) tx = clamp(p.x + Math.sign(awayX) * 100, 80, 900);\n    }\n    if ((core.state === 'flight' || core.state === 'return') && dist(p, core) < 120 && !cannon) {\n      ty = wrap(p.y + (dy(p.y, core.y) >= 0 ? 120 : -120));\n      tx = clamp(p.x + (p.x >= core.x ? 60 : -60), 80, 900);\n     if scenario=='server':\n      check('hub server: host has two player bodies only',any(w.get('net',{}).get('steps',0)>0 and len(w.get('s',{}).get('players',[]))==2 for w in worlds))\n     # No activity after hub end: exact tick and sends remain unchanged.\n     before=worlds\n     page.wait_for_timeout(350)\n     after=[]\n     for f in page.frames[1:]:\n      try:after.append(f.evaluate('({s:window.RuinApp?.game?.debug?.snapshot(),net:window.RuinApp?.online?.debug})'))\n      except Exception:pass\n     check(f'hub {players} {scenario}: no simulation or sends after end',len(before)==len(after) and all(b.get('s',{}).get('tick')==a.get('s',{}).get('tick') and b.get('net',{}).get('sent')==a.get('net',{}).get('sent') for b,a in zip(before,after)))\n     (ART/f'hub-{players}-{scenario}.json').write_text(json.dumps({'report':report,'errors':errors,'warnings':warnings,'worlds':worlds},indent=2))\n     context.close()\n    if '--official-only' not in sys.argv and '--campaign-only' not in sys.argv:\n     for scenario in ['nonhost-leave','visibility']:\n      context=browser.new_context(viewport={'width':1280,'height':860});page=context.new_page();errors=[]\n      page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)))\n      page.goto(base+'/'+DEV.name+f'/vendor/hub/harness.html?game={GAME}&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&limit=120')\n      page.wait_for_function(\"document.querySelectorAll('iframe').length===2\")\n      page.wait_for_function(\"[...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].every(f=>f.contentWindow.RuinApp?.online)\")\n      page.locator('#release').click()\n      page.wait_for_function(\"[...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].every(f=>f.contentWindow.AIHub.time()>=0)\")\n      page.wait_for_timeout(700)\n      frames=page.frames[1:];host=frames[0]\n      if scenario=='nonhost-leave':\n       old=host.evaluate('RuinApp.world.tick')\n       page.locator('#who').select_option('p1');page.locator('#remove').click()\n       page.wait_for_function(\"document.querySelector('iframe').contentWindow.RuinApp.world.players[1].departed===true\")\n       page.wait_for_timeout(500)\n       state=host.evaluate('({tick:RuinApp.world.tick,players:RuinApp.world.players,net:RuinApp.online.debug})')\n       check('hub explicit non-host departure: remaining scout continues',state['tick']>old and state['players'][0]['alive'] and state['players'][1]['departed'] and state['players'][1]['respawn']==0)\n       page.locator('#timeup').click()\n       page.wait_for_function(\"document.querySelector('#round').textContent.includes('Ended played')\")\n       check('hub explicit non-host departure: host submits valid surviving standings','Red Fox' in page.locator('#round').inner_text() and 'Blue Otter' not in page.locator('#round').inner_text())\n      else:\n       old=host.evaluate('RuinApp.world.tick');page.locator('#hide').click();page.wait_for_timeout(1200)\n       hidden=host.evaluate('RuinApp.world.tick');page.locator('#hide').click();page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n       shown=host.evaluate('RuinApp.world.tick')\n       check('hub short host visibility loss continues authoritative simulation',hidden>old+80 and shown>hidden)\n       page.locator('#hide').click()\n       page.wait_for_function(\"document.querySelector('#round').textContent.includes('Ended void (host-hidden)')\",timeout=25000)\n       check('hub over-20s host hidden follows void ownership','host-hidden' in page.locator('#round').inner_text())\n       before=host.evaluate('({tick:RuinApp.world.tick,sent:RuinApp.online.debug.sent})');page.locator('#hide').click();page.wait_for_timeout(500)\n       after=host.evaluate('({tick:RuinApp.world.tick,sent:RuinApp.online.debug.sent})')\n       check('hub void round never resumes on visibility return',before==after)\n      check('hub '+scenario+': no page errors',not errors,str(errors))\n      (ART/f'hub-{scenario}.json').write_text(json.dumps({'round':page.locator('#round').inner_text(),'errors':errors},indent=2))\n      context.close()\n    if '--campaign' in sys.argv or '--campaign-only' in sys.argv:\n     for scenario in ['standard','server']:\n      context=browser.new_context(viewport={'width':1280,'height':860});page=context.new_page();errors=[]\n      page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)))\n      page.goto(base+'/'+DEV.name+f'/vendor/hub/harness.html?game={GAME}&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&limit=300&scenario={scenario}&seed=1982')\n      count=3 if scenario=='server' else 2\n      page.wait_for_function(f\"document.querySelectorAll('iframe').length==={count}\")\n      page.wait_for_function(\"[...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].every(f=>f.contentWindow.RuinApp?.online)\")\n      frames=page.frames[1:]\n      for f in frames:\n       f.evaluate(\"\"\"() => {if(AIHub.server)return;RuinApp.controls.frames=()=>{const app=RuinApp,w=app.online.getWorld(),i=app.online.localIndex;return [RuinSim.pilot(w,i)];};}\"\"\")\n      page.locator('#release').click()\n      timeout_error=None\n      try:page.wait_for_function(\"[...document.querySelectorAll('iframe')].find(f=>f.contentWindow.AIHub.isHost)?.contentWindow.RuinApp.online.finished===true\",timeout=210000)\n      except Exception as e:timeout_error=str(e)\n      page.wait_for_timeout(2600)\n      worlds=[]\n      for f in frames:\n       try:worlds.append(f.evaluate('({host:AIHub.isHost,server:!!AIHub.server,s:RuinApp.game.debug.snapshot(),net:RuinApp.online.debug})'))\n       except Exception:pass\n      host_state=next((w for w in worlds if w['host']),{})\n      check('hub '+scenario+' full campaign uses ordinary actions to win',not timeout_error and host_state.get('s',{}).get('mode')=='victory',str(timeout_error or host_state.get('s',{}).get('stats')))\n      check('hub '+scenario+' campaign visits all sectors and strikes airborne heart',host_state.get('s',{}).get('sector')==2 and host_state.get('s',{}).get('stats',{}).get('coreHits')==6 and host_state.get('s',{}).get('stats',{}).get('airborne',0)>0)\n      check('hub '+scenario+' campaign ends with matching authoritative score and outcome',bool(worlds) and all(w.get('s',{}).get('score')==host_state.get('s',{}).get('score') and w.get('s',{}).get('mode')=='victory' and w.get('s',{}).get('ended') for w in worlds))\n      check('hub '+scenario+' campaign reports one host finish',host_state.get('net',{}).get('finishCalls')==1 and all(w.get('net',{}).get('finishCalls')==0 for w in worlds if not w.get('host')))\n      check('hub '+scenario+' campaign has no runtime errors',not errors,str(errors))\n      (ART/f'hub-campaign-{scenario}.json').write_text(json.dumps({'worlds':worlds,'errors':errors,'round':page.locator('#round').inner_text()},indent=2))\n      context.close()\n   finally:browser.close()\n finally:server.shutdown();server.server_close()\n (ART/'hub-browser-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(results,indent=2))\n return results\nif __name__=='__main__':\n result=run()\n for x in result:\n  if not x['pass']:print('FAIL '+x['name']+' '+x.get('detail',''))\n print(json.dumps({'passed':sum(x['pass'] for x in result),'failed':sum(not x['pass'] for x in result)}))\n sys.exit(any(not x['pass'] for x in result))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
