{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/.npmrc <<'EOF'\nloglevel=silent\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nroot=pathlib.Path('.')\nr={\n'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-06 02:29:04','source':'Yars’ Revenge (Atari, 1982; Howard Scott Warshaw)','plan':'PLAN.md','genre':'Arcade siege shooter','perspective':'Fixed overhead x/y arena with decorative height','tech':'JavaScript; my-3D2dge 0.89.1 (8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691); AI Hub Protocol 1 client 1.4.0 (35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869); Canvas2D; Web Audio; dependency-free Node build','artDirection':'Original dimensional procedural pixel art: articulated insects, cellular fortress, layered cosmic ruins, emissive static and material ramps','animation':'Native pixel/body draw pattern with mathematical articulated posing, wing beats, mandibles, fortress transformations, particles, light and procedural collapse','audio':'Code-only three-sector music motifs, oscillator/noise effects and formant gibberish voices; first-run music10%; separate master/music/effects/voice buses','online':'Standalone solo and simultaneous local1–2 co-op; AI Hub host-authoritative online1–2 shared-world co-op, including dedicated server host; no standalone matchmaking','testing':'Unrestricted headless rules/browser verification; Playwright1.63.0 Chromium and WebKit, standard gamepad stubs, CDP multitouch, offline audio, two-page and dedicated-server Hub harness; physical controller, touchscreen, TV and iOS hardware unavailable','research':'Atari original instructions and animated gameplay excerpt; AtariAge manual; publisher retrospectives; creator interview; pack-in comic story page. Full longplay failure/progression and airborne-kill footage not independently observed; documented in docs/research.md','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux / Ubuntu26.04 WSL2','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra','usage':'added on import'},\n 'testingFeedback':['7 distinct defects found and fixed during rule, browser and lifecycle verification; test-fixture mistakes are counted separately. See docs/testing.md.','1 critical multiplayer lifecycle defect: completion could overtake the final state under latency. An acknowledged outcome handoff now precedes the single host finish.','The ordinary-action full campaign and empty-shell final respawn/refill/interception tests; they prove that all phases remain winnable without cheats.','A syntax-only check: it passed while menu clipping and a network outcome-ordering defect still existed. Actual rendered and lifecycle checks found those.'],\n 'engineFeedback':['The dependency-free native pixel primitives, dimensional shading, fixed-step advance and built-in Shell/input/settings.','Yes: TV Shell scaling made CSS dimensions larger than expected; initial menu controls clipped. A debug snapshot also accidentally let a cosmetic attract flag shadow the live mode.','The deterministic siege simulation: persistent cellular shields, contact energy, remote friendly-danger cannon, fortress state machine and co-op authority.','Coordinating the native scene/menu clock with independent authoritative online ticking and cosmetic event cleanup across replay.','None. The imported engine is unchanged; game-specific systems and UI styling extend its public APIs.','A compact shared-world reference with dedicated-server ticking, reliable action acknowledgements and an outcome-state handoff would reduce integration work.'],\n 'promptFeedback':['Concrete source relationships and playable acceptance gates kept the vertical slice coherent.','The brief’s final output paths were authoritative; the plan’s relative paths were internal suggestions. No unresolved ambiguity remains.','Finishing the same campaign across solo, co-op, touch, dev tools and authoritative online lifecycle while keeping one portable HTML.','Keep the core acceptance gates, and distinguish mandatory release checks from optional exploratory breadth more explicitly.'],\n 'aiHub':{'name':'Yars of Ruin','tagline':'A tiny living weapon. An enormous last reply.','description':'Bite through colossal cellular defenses and feed their stolen energy to a rail-mounted siege cannon. Free the swarm across three stations, alone or with another scout, and intercept the final airborne heart.','type':'Game','genre':'Shooter','source':'Yars’ Revenge (1982)','series':'','players':'1–2','controls':'Left stick / WASD: fly; right stick / mouse: aim; R2 / left click: fire; contact: bite; L2 / Space / right click: cannon; Options / Esc: pause; touch: invisible move/aim sticks and contextual cannon.','tags':['arcade','co-op','top-down','pixel art','sci-fi','boss fights']}}\n(root/'exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=root/'Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/tools/build.mjs'\ns=p.read_text();a=s.index('let report=');b=s.index('const html=',a);s=s[:a]+\\\"const report=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root,'..','exit-interview.json'),'utf8'));\\\\n\\\"+s[b:];p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
