{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"agent_message","text":"The packaged solo campaign passes through to victory. Visual review caught a phone-specific engine defect: its minimum scale cropped the arena, leaving the fortress offscreen. I’m patching that sizing rule and adding an assertion that the whole arena fits on small screens.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport difflib,json\nD=Path('Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904');p=D/'vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js';old=p.read_text();s=old.replace(\\\"this.S = fill ? Math.max(1, fit) : Math.max(1, Math.min(Math.floor(pw / fix[0]), Math.floor(ph / fix[1])));\\\", \\\"// Local small-screen-fit patch: a fixed arena must remain visible below 1x.\\\\n      this.S = fit < 1 ? fit : fill ? fit : Math.max(1, Math.min(Math.floor(pw / fix[0]), Math.floor(ph / fix[1])));\\\")\nassert s\"'!=old;p.write_text(s);(D/'\"'vendor/engine/small-screen-fit.patch').write_text(''.join(difflib.unified_diff(old.splitlines(keepends=True),s.splitlines(keepends=True),fromfile='a/my-3d2dge.js',tofile='b/my-3d2dge.js')))\np=D/'src/presentation/render.js';s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"E.tones(p.color||(p.color||PLAYER[(p.index||0)%2]))\\\", \\\"E.tones(p.color||PLAYER[(p.index||0)%2])\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=D/'tests/browser.py';s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"    x=ev('RuinApp.world.players[0].x');touches('touchStart'\\\", \\\"    check('phone framing keeps whole fixed arena on screen',lambda:ev('__game.screen.OX>=0 && __game.screen.OY>=0 && __game.screen.W*__game.screen.S<=__game.screen.canvas.width+.1 && __game.screen.H*__game.screen.S<=__game.screen.canvas.height+.1'))\\\\n    x=ev('RuinApp.world.players[0].x');touches('touchStart'\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('exit-interview.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text());r['testingFeedback'][0]='8 distinct defects found and fixed during rule, browser and lifecycle verification; test-fixture mistakes are counted separately. See docs/testing.md.';r['testingFeedback'][1]='2 critical defects: a multiplayer completion could overtake its final state under latency, and native minimum1x scaling cropped the fortress on small phones. Both have regression coverage.';r['engineFeedback'][4]='Patched Screen.resize fixed-resolution scaling to allow fractional fit below1x. The native minimum1x cropped a960px arena on390px phones. Patch and pristine imported revision are retained in vendor/engine and docs/provenance.md.';r['sourceInformation']['tech']=r['sourceInformation']['tech'].replace('my-3D2dge 0.89.1 (','my-3D2dge 0.89.1 plus small-screen-fit patch (');p.write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nwith (D/'docs/provenance.md').open('a')as f:f.write('''\\\\n## Local engine patch\\\\n\\\\n\"'`vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js` changes one sizing assignment in `Screen.resize`: fixed-resolution content may scale below1x when its buffer is larger than the physical canvas. Upstream clamps every scale to at least1, which produced negative letterbox offsets and cropped the fortress on a390px phone. The patched branch uses the actual fractional fit only below1x; normal desktop integer/fill scaling is unchanged. The exact diff is retained in `vendor/engine/small-screen-fit.patch`; the pinned `engine-upstream` checkout remains pristine. The phone browser test now asserts nonnegative offsets and that the entire buffer fits the canvas. No other engine changes.'\"\\\\n''')\nPY\nnode Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/tools/build.mjs\n/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/tests/browser.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
