{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_89","type":"agent_message","text":"The final input review found and fixed three more issues: WASD could override mouse aim, co-op could leave the sole controller assigned away from the title menu, and transition settings did not open. Regression checks pass for all three. The standalone suite now has 55 passing checks, including the full campaign, ending, phone framing, and touch cleanup.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_90","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nD=pathlib.Path('Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904')\np=pathlib.Path('exit-interview.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text());r['testingFeedback'][0]='12 distinct defects found and fixed during rule, rendered UX, input and lifecycle verification; test-fixture mistakes are excluded. See docs/testing.md.';r['testingFeedback'][1]='3 critical defects: completion could overtake the final multiplayer state; minimum1x scaling cropped the fortress on phones; one-pad co-op could strand controller navigation after quitting. All are fixed and regression-tested.';p.write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=D/'src/main.js';s=p.read_text();old=\\\"const pages=[['Source Information · 1 / 3',info.slice(0,5)],['Source Information · 2 / 3',info.slice(5,10)],['Source Information · 3 / 3',info.slice(10)],['Testing Feedback',tests],['Engine Feedback · 1 / 2',engine.slice(0,3)],['Engine Feedback · 2 / 2',engine.slice(3)],['Prompt Feedback',prompt]];\\\";new=\\\"const pages=[['Source Information · 1 / 4',info.slice(0,5)],['Source Information · 2 / 4',info.slice(5,8)],['Source Information · 3 / 4',info.slice(8,11)],['Source Information · 4 / 4',info.slice(11)],['Testing Feedback · 1 / 2',tests.slice(0,2)],['Testing Feedback · 2 / 2',tests.slice(2)],['Engine Feedback · 1 / 2',engine.slice(0,3)],['Engine Feedback · 2 / 2',engine.slice(3)],['Prompt Feedback · 1 / 2',prompt.slice(0,2)],['Prompt Feedback · 2 / 2',prompt.slice(2)]];\\\";assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new);p.write_text(s)\np=D/'tests/browser.py';s=p.read_text().replace('Source Information · 1 / 3','Source Information · 1 / 4').replace(\\\"    # Actual packaged scene/update/input route, ordinary actions, all transitions and ending.\\\\n\\\", \\\"    page.set_viewport_size({'width':1920,'height':1080});ev('__game.screen.resize()')\\\\n    # Actual packaged scene/update/input route, ordinary actions, all transitions and ending.\\\\n\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=D/'README.md';s=p.read_text().replace('with a player host and a dedicated server host under latency, jitter and loss','with a player host under150ms latency/50ms jitter/5% loss, and a hidden dedicated server with ordinary sampled remote controls under0added network impairment');p.write_text(s)\np=D/'docs/testing.md';s=p.read_text().replace('Eight distinct defects','Twelve distinct defects');s=s.replace('## Evidence interpretation','''|9|WASD could override independent held mouse aim.|Mouse aiming now follows explicit aim ownership; combinedWASD/held-mouse regression.|\n|10|One-pad co-op could strand title/menu control onP2.|Title restores single-player device ownership; either scout’s controller can navigate pause. Actual stub regression coversP2pause/resume and title activation after quit. Critical.|\n|11|Sector-clear Pause/settings action opened no menu.|Transition now opens the real native Settings screen and returns to the transition; packaged campaign assertion.|\n|12|Custom touch pointers survived visibility loss.|Visibility and menu transitions clear ownership; actual concurrent-touch visibility regression.|\n\n## Actual online full-play conditions\n\nThe two-player host campaign completed under150ms latency,50ms jitter and5% loss, with matching victory/score on both copies. The dedicated-server campaign completed with its engine/render loop stopped and canvas hidden, with both remote players sending ordinary controls; added transport impairment was0for this full-play run. Its stateful test controller used read-only host awareness for planning, with no life, charge, damage or outcome mutations. Separate official dedicated-server stress checks used150/50/5, so progression proof and transport stress are not conflated. The sampled-controller suite also proves quantized100–150ms action holds and up to100ms input delay in the actual simulation.\n\n## Evidence interpretation''');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncommand -v biome\nbiome check --write --linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/src Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/tools Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/tests/*.mjs Yars-of-Ruin-Yars-Revenge-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022904/tests/server-pilot.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
